# Local environment for the static analyzer.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in real values:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed. This file is the committed
# template and is safe to share - it contains no real values.

# ---- UI ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 0 to disable the PDCurses results browser and print straight to the
# terminal (useful for CI, piping to a file, or debugging).
STATIC_ANALYZER_CURSES=1

# ---- External tools -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Directory holding the .yar/.yara rule files. Defaults to <project>/yara-rules.
# YARA_RULES_DIR=C:/Users/The4thReich/Desktop/IAProject/yara-rules

# Path to the Cminer binary. Falls back to invoking it through WSL.
# CMINER_PATH=

# ---- CTI threat intel ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to skip the CTI lookup phase entirely.
CTI_SKIP=0

# Optional JSON overlay for the CTI pipeline:
#   {"keys":{...},"endpoints":{...},"cache_dir":"...","offline":false,
#    "disabled_providers":["crtsh"],"dns_record_types":["A"], ...}
# Every provider base URL is overridable, which is what lets the pipeline be pointed
# at a proxy or at a local test server without recompiling. Unknown keys are ignored
# and an unreadable file is reported as a warning instead of aborting the run.
# tests/cti_test_config.json + tests/fake_cti_server.py are a working example.
# CTI_CONFIG=cti_test_config.json

# ---- Diagnostics --------------------------------------------------------------------
# When set, the trace layer writes symbol/offset diagnostics to this file.
# TRACE_FILE=

# ---- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CTI keys can be pulled from a running `bw serve` so they never rest on disk.
# The analyzer GETs /object/secure-item/vault-item on loopback, matches the
# items you name exactly, and reads login.password only of those that also
# name a target - no other item is ever touched. This pass is loopback-only, so
# it also runs when CTI_SKIP=1 (which only disables the internet lookups); with
# nothing configured below, the CTI phase behaves exactly as before.
#
# CTI_BW_KEYS is a comma-separated roster of "VaultItem=ENV_TARGET" entries. A
# bare "VaultItem" only checks that the vault holds such an item - its secret is
# never read. A key found in the vault is applied to its ENV_TARGET for the
# lifetime of the process only, then unset. A key that is not in the vault is
# reported as missing, so the roster doubles as a "which keys do I still have
# to add" checklist.
#
# Once per shell session, before running:
#     bw login
#     export BW_SESSION=$(bw unlock --raw)
#     bw sync
#     bw serve
#
# CTI_BW_KEYS=VirusTotal=VT_API_KEY,AbuseIPDB=ABUSEIPDB_API_KEY,AlienVault OTX=OTX_API_KEY,abuse.ch=ABUSECH_AUTH_KEY,GreyNoise=GREYNOISE_API_KEY,NVD=NVD_API_KEY
# CTI_BW_SERVE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8087
#
# Legacy single-key form, still supported:
# CTI_KEY_NAME=VirusTotal
# CTI_KEY_TARGET=VT_API_KEY
#
# Without the vault, the providers read these variables directly:
# ABUSEIPDB_API_KEY, OTX_API_KEY, VT_API_KEY (or VIRUSTOTAL_API_KEY),
# ABUSECH_AUTH_KEY (or ABUSECH_API_KEY), GREYNOISE_API_KEY, NVD_API_KEY.
#
# Only the first four are needed for their providers to run. GreyNoise is
# queried through its Community API and NVD through its public API: both answer
# without credentials, so leaving GREYNOISE_API_KEY / NVD_API_KEY unset simply
# means fewer requests per minute, never a skipped provider. The remaining
# providers (Shodan InternetDB, RDAP, DNS-over-HTTPS, crt.sh, CIRCL hashlookup,
# EPSS, CISA KEV, ATT&CK) never need a key at all.
#
# Published free-tier limits, so the built-in rates are not a surprise:
#   * GreyNoise Community API - 10 IP lookups per day unauthenticated; the free
#     tier needs a business e-mail and allows 50 lookups per week. That daily
#     figure is why the keyless rate is one lookup every five minutes.
#   * NVD public API - 5 requests / 30 s unauthenticated, 50 / 30 s with a key.
#     Over the limit NVD answers HTTP 403; a key that is invalid gets a 404 with
#     an empty body, which the report calls out separately.
#   * AbuseIPDB - the free tier allows 1000 check requests per day.
#   * abuse.ch Community API (ThreatFox / URLhaus / MalwareBazaar) - free of
#     charge under the fair use principles, but an Auth-Key is required.
#
# Prefer the vault over writing keys into this file. If you do keep a key here,
# .env is gitignored, but it is still plaintext on disk.
